{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4","id":1307929,"title":"Hanging spells (Time 4)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-25T20:18:03-07:00","id":1307929,"title":"Hanging spells (Time 4)","content":"Hi, give ideas of uses for the Time 4 effect of hanging spells, besides hanging buffs with maximum successes to be used quickly.<br /> <br /> Also, we have examples of effects with duration bigger than a turn that can change after it is cast. In HDYDT there are examples where the mage shapshift into some animal that can breath fire, or engulf his body in elecricity or even teleport at will (no need for another spell). We also have wards, that is active and trigger some other effect when some condition is met (like some kind of patter of Force,Life,Matter, etc. entering/touching/etc.), all of them work without Time 4 (except for one kind of ward).<br /> <br /> Having said that, couldn't the mage use shapeshift to give himslef the ability to buff at will?<br /> <br /> For example: Let's say the mage wants to use Life 3 to turn his skin into a thick leather, making it able to soak lethal, whenever he wants. He must cast a Time 4 spell to hang this effect until he needs. <br /> OR he could just do like the shapeshift example an turn into a human being that is able to thick his skin at will, instead of the fire breathing tiger, using only Life sphere.<br /> <br /> Why would anyone use Time 4 in an effect, then? Am I missing something here?<br /> <br /> Dunno if I did explain it right..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T22:31:30-07:00","id":1307962,"title":"","content":"Implanting spells into shapeshifted forms certainly is an edge case, really. I guess it boils down to paradigm. *And* it is limited to implanting effects onto beings that these beings can then trigger on *themselves*. Hung spells are way more flexible.<br /> <br /> Now, on the topic of Wards, you can't just put any effect on a Ward/Ban. Their primary function is to encourage things to stay away from an area through various described methods, to block them outright, or to banish/lock spirits. Hung spells are, again, way more flexible than that.<br /> <br /> Now, why you would use Time 4 in an effect?<br /> <br /> First off, hung spells can be tied to a trigger. It doesn't need to be an active decision by the Mage to trigger the spell - it can be caused by any event, if you have the according Sphere(s) to tie it to the circumstance.<br /> This is *big* for any kind of automatically triggered defensive spells for example - and unlike permanently running defense spells, are potentially less obvious to those that can see ongoing magicks.<br /> Heck, they can trigger at the time your mage is asleep in their bed, unconcious, has sensory impairments or is simply *too wounded* to properly perform their practice without difficulty increases.<br /> And again, neither the spell nor the automatic trigger need to be actually put on your mage. Having an enemy as a temporary ally, and wanna make sure they don't backstab you? Time 4 spell with a trigger to make them melt as soon as they try to attack you. Traps around your sanctum? Done. Want to put 'special' safety into your car that magically keeps you from harm in case you crash? Done. Car's too precious to get a scratch? Have a hung spell that triggers as soon as the car *would* be about to crash and stops it.<br /> <br /> And those are just the examples dealing with damage or damage prevention. Hung spells can be about anything.<br /> <br /> Second, as example'd above, hung spells can not only be put onto your Mage, but also...pretty much anything else. Places, forces, objects, combinations thereof. With a trigger, again, to make the spell trigger under specific circumstances.<br /> <br /> Third, the hung spell *does not count against your one-Arete-roll-per-round limit*. You can trigger the Time 4'd spell in the same round you do an Arete roll. Or several. Like Wonders. With preparation, you can let out a barrage of effects at once. Or tie multiple to anything else to trigger all at once - or in series.<br /> <br /> Fourth, Time 4 hung spells have, aside of Time 4, no other strict requirements. You are not bound to also take Sphere X or Y - it entirely depends on what your character usually does. No *need* for Correspondence like with Wards. No *need* for Life like in shapeshifting. You're completely free to hang *any* kind of spell that you could do before with your sphere setup already, and for the purpose you previously used it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-26-2019, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T11:22:41-07:00","id":1308071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1307962#post1307962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Implanting spells into shapeshifted forms certainly is an edge case, really. I guess it boils down to paradigm. *And* it is limited to implanting effects onto beings that these beings can then trigger on *themselves*. Hung spells are way more flexible.<br /> <br /> Now, on the topic of Wards, you can't just put any effect on a Ward/Ban. Their primary function is to encourage things to stay away from an area through various described methods, to block them outright, or to banish/lock spirits. Hung spells are, again, way more flexible than that.<br /> <br /> Now, why you would use Time 4 in an effect?<br /> <br /> First off, hung spells can be tied to a trigger. It doesn't need to be an active decision by the Mage to trigger the spell - it can be caused by any event, if you have the according Sphere(s) to tie it to the circumstance.<br /> This is *big* for any kind of automatically triggered defensive spells for example - and unlike permanently running defense spells, are potentially less obvious to those that can see ongoing magicks.<br /> Heck, they can trigger at the time your mage is asleep in their bed, unconcious, has sensory impairments or is simply *too wounded* to properly perform their practice without difficulty increases.<br /> And again, neither the spell nor the automatic trigger need to be actually put on your mage. Having an enemy as a temporary ally, and wanna make sure they don't backstab you? Time 4 spell with a trigger to make them melt as soon as they try to attack you. Traps around your sanctum? Done. Want to put 'special' safety into your car that magically keeps you from harm in case you crash? Done. Car's too precious to get a scratch? Have a hung spell that triggers as soon as the car *would* be about to crash and stops it.<br /> <br /> And those are just the examples dealing with damage or damage prevention. Hung spells can be about anything.<br /> <br /> Second, as example'd above, hung spells can not only be put onto your Mage, but also...pretty much anything else. Places, forces, objects, combinations thereof. With a trigger, again, to make the spell trigger under specific circumstances.<br /> <br /> Third, the hung spell *does not count against your one-Arete-roll-per-round limit*. You can trigger the Time 4'd spell in the same round you do an Arete roll. Or several. Like Wonders. With preparation, you can let out a barrage of effects at once. Or tie multiple to anything else to trigger all at once - or in series.<br /> <br /> Fourth, Time 4 hung spells have, aside of Time 4, no other strict requirements. You are not bound to also take Sphere X or Y - it entirely depends on what your character usually does. No *need* for Correspondence like with Wards. No *need* for Life like in shapeshifting. You're completely free to hang *any* kind of spell that you could do before with your sphere setup already, and for the purpose you previously used it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for answering, those are very nice points. But maybe some, or all, of them could be replicated without Time 4. Wards and shapeshifting were just examples of spells that change their behavior after they are cast.<br /> <br /> We have rotes of healing with duration, where a pool of dice is used to heal for a duration whenever the mage is hurt. This is independent if he mage is awake, incapacitated or too wounded.<br /> We have rotes where the target talks gibberish whenever he is interrogated. The effect is always on, but just changes behavior when something happens (the target can speak normally, just can't when interrogated).<br /> <br /> All that without Time 4. So what is stopping some mage to cast a persistent effect that changes when he wants, or when he is hurted (Life), etc?<br /> <br /> All the benefits you posted coul happen in an &quot;always running&quot; effect that changes after casted..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T11:47:30-07:00","id":1308077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1308071#post1308071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for answering, those are very nice points. But maybe some, or all, of them could be replicated without Time 4. Wards and shapeshifting were just examples of spells that change their behavior after they are cast.<br /> <br /> We have rotes of healing with duration, where a pool of dice is used to heal for a duration whenever the mage is hurt. This is independent if he mage is awake, incapacitated or too wounded.<br /> We have rotes where the target talks gibberish whenever he is interrogated. The effect is always on, but just changes behavior when something happens (the target can speak normally, just can't when interrogated).<br /> <br /> All that without Time 4. So what is stopping some mage to cast a persistent effect that changes when he wants, or when he is hurted (Life), etc?<br /> <br /> All the benefits you posted coul happen in an &quot;always running&quot; effect that changes after casted..</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you link to a rote that does the long-running healing as you mentioned?<br /> <br /> I'd treat any of the always running with a trigger effects (the interrogation) as Time 4 + Mind 2 or 3 or require continual recasting or a supply of quintessence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":15603,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","user":"PhillyCuriosity","date":". 04-26-2019, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T11:52:27-07:00","id":1308080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1308071#post1308071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have rotes of healing with duration, where a pool of dice is used to heal for a duration whenever the mage is hurt. This is independent if he mage is awake, incapacitated or too wounded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is a thing that can be tied into the whole 'shapeshifting effects into people', yes. But, speaking of people, or rather...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We have rotes where the target </div> </div> </div>Targets! They make all the difference. In your example case, if I wanted to put an effect with lots of successes onto a target without Time 4, I'd either 1) Need some time and potentially a willing target, or 2) Some time and a potentially unwilling target that can't stop me or 3) Correspondence to do it from afar, *and* at a high enough level to get the other spheres through the correspondence connection.<br /> <br /> Orrr....I hang the spell with Time 4 and a lot of stored successes prepared in my Sanctum, and I apply the whole shebang instantly with a literal slap. While also casting another effect at them at the same time just for good measure.<br /> <br /> Or heck, setting an instant, prepared high-success trap on some ground I happen to run by by spitting at it. No need to stop. All's prepared in the Sanctum, and I didn't even have to know beforehand where I put it - I just needed to mix Matter as a locking sphere into the preparation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> And even when you have yourself as a target, some effects can't be quite put on you with a duration. Imagine a spell that teleports you home as soon as you're direly wounded. Spells shapeshifted into you can be manually triggered or have a duration, but you can't always count on winning the initiative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-26-2019, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T14:02:00-07:00","id":1308114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PhillyCuriosity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1308077#post1308077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you link to a rote that does the long-running healing as you mentioned?<br /> <br /> I'd treat any of the always running with a trigger effects (the interrogation) as Time 4 + Mind 2 or 3 or require continual recasting or a supply of quintessence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look for Gift of Prana rote of Euthanatos. The interrogation one is Encrypt and doesn't need Time 4","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T14:04:25-07:00","id":1308115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1308080#post1308080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is a thing that can be tied into the whole 'shapeshifting effects into people', yes. But, speaking of people, or rather...<br /> <br /> Targets! They make all the difference. In your example case, if I wanted to put an effect with lots of successes onto a target without Time 4, I'd either 1) Need some time and potentially a willing target, or 2) Some time and a potentially unwilling target that can't stop me or 3) Correspondence to do it from afar, *and* at a high enough level to get the other spheres through the correspondence connection.<br /> <br /> Orrr....I hang the spell with Time 4 and a lot of stored successes prepared in my Sanctum, and I apply the whole shebang instantly with a literal slap. While also casting another effect at them at the same time just for good measure.<br /> <br /> Or heck, setting an instant, prepared high-success trap on some ground I happen to run by by spitting at it. No need to stop. All's prepared in the Sanctum, and I didn't even have to know beforehand where I put it - I just needed to mix Matter as a locking sphere into the preparation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> And even when you have yourself as a target, some effects can't be quite put on you with a duration. Imagine a spell that teleports you home as soon as you're direly wounded. Spells shapeshifted into you can be manually triggered or have a duration, but you can't always count on winning the initiative.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't get it. Why the running effect can't be casted beforehand in your sanctum and the hung spell can?<br /> <br /> Can you give examples?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T14:19:31-07:00","id":1308119,"title":"","content":"The running effect that you cast on yourself can be done in your Sanctum, sure! That's not the problem.<br /> <br /> But how are you going to cast a spell on somebody from your Sanctum without high levels of Correspondence? And if you don't have correspondence and you are in the heat of conflict, how are you going to cast a spell that requires a lot of successes without taking several rounds of casting time? How are you going to prepare a trap spell in your Sanctum if you don't even know yet what you might be putting it onto?<br /> And how would these spells be 'running' while you haven't applied them to a target yet? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That's exactly a thing Time 4 *does*. It hangs a spell until you instantly use it on something, or it gets triggered by an event.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T15:22:53-07:00","id":1308138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1308119#post1308119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The running effect that you cast on yourself can be done in your Sanctum, sure! That's not the problem.<br /> <br /> But how are you going to cast a spell on somebody from your Sanctum without high levels of Correspondence? And if you don't have correspondence and you are in the heat of conflict, how are you going to cast a spell that requires a lot of successes without taking several rounds of casting time? How are you going to prepare a trap spell in your Sanctum if you don't even know yet what you might be putting it onto?<br /> And how would these spells be 'running' while you haven't applied them to a target yet? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That's exactly a thing Time 4 *does*. It hangs a spell until you instantly use it on something, or it gets triggered by an event.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still don't understand the difference between the two. Why can you cast a trap or affect another target with Time 4 and not with running effects?<br /> <br /> With Time 4 you also don't know yet where you are going to put the trap spell. Can yoj explain better?<br /> <br /> Also, this means that only the effects where you don't know the target yet can't be made. Normal buffs or similar effects that affect you, or some object (or friend) that you have access to can be done and that's 80% of Time 4 hung spells, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T15:55:51-07:00","id":1308153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1308138#post1308138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I still don't understand the difference between the two. Why can you cast a trap or affect another target with Time 4 and not with running effects?<br /> <br /> With Time 4 you also don't know yet where you are going to put the trap spell. Can yoj explain better?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because with Time 4, you can cast a spell before applying it to a target. The spell is rolled, hung, but not 'running' yet. A running spell needs its target during casting time, because...well, it's running from the moment it is cast, so it's already applied to a target.<br /> Think of Time 4'd spells as storing an already roll'd spell on your hotbar for later use in this case ;p<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T13:05:56-07:00","id":1308374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1308153#post1308153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because with Time 4, you can cast a spell before applying it to a target. The spell is rolled, hung, but not 'running' yet. A running spell needs its target during casting time, because...well, it's running from the moment it is cast, so it's already applied to a target.<br /> Think of Time 4'd spells as storing an already roll'd spell on your hotbar for later use in this case ;p</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Bassically offensive spells or the ones that affects targets that you don't have contact yet. Like a fireball. Could you provide more examples? You think that there is no way to do this with persistent effects, maybe by inputting the information needed afterwards, like pointing at the target? <br /> <br /> And I don't know, buff self or allies and enchanting items are most of the uses of rituals that demand lots of successes. The majority of the uses of Time 4 can be done without it..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 04-27-2019, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T21:23:46-07:00","id":1308420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1308374#post1308374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see. Bassically offensive spells or the ones that affects targets that you don't have contact yet. Like a fireball. Could you provide more examples? You think that there is no way to do this with persistent effects, maybe by inputting the information needed afterwards, like pointing at the target?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends.<br /> In this example, the fire breathing example of 'shapeshifted' spells works fine - you do a normal dexterity + .&lt;something&gt; roll to target it, since you also don't use an Arete roll for it. You simply happen to breathe fire, and it's essentially the same as holding a flamethrower weapon in your mouth - it essentially emulates something else that normally wouldn't require an arete roll. Same goes for the shapeshifted ability of forming extra armor or the electricity example from the book.<br /> <br /> Really, I think the simplest way of putting Time 4 is &quot;Time 4 allows you to store the results of an effect's Arete roll in a trigger without running the actual effect yet.&quot;. As for more examples...I've given so many in the course of this thread, I think we're just running in circles now. Perhaps somebody else wants to jump in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T02:14:29-07:00","id":1308443,"title":"","content":"It's worth remembering that every Effect a mage has active - all the ones they are &quot;concentrating&quot; on - count towards how difficult it will be to cast additional Effects. Every two simultaneous Effects make the next Effect accrue a +1 difficulty. Hence why Mages don't always have a huge list of Effects they cover themselves with every morning. One or two, maybe. Really, any more than one makes creating Effects in the moment more difficult, and the mage never truly knows all that they'll need beforehand.<br /> <br /> By virtue of being Time 4, a hung effect does not apply here. The Effect isn't present but dormant, like a high-duration one. It exists outside the flow of time entirely, much like an object or creature can be so removed at the same level of mastery. It's not <i>there</i>, until it is.<br /> <br /> This also makes hung Effects harder to detect and, more important, <i>unweaved</i>. A constant Effect is like a beacon to anyone with magickal senses. That makes the Effect vulnerable to attempts to dispel it. Even someone without Prime knowledge could notice some magick is going on, either through other Sphere senses (&quot;the person's biology seems weird somehow&quot;) or through logical deduction given evidence. Hung spells are less likely to be noticed even by the mystically sensitive, because there's no Effect to sense. Yet. Only someone with knowledge of Time could reasonably be expected to spot the irregular knot in the timestream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T13:08:06-07:00","id":1308512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1308420#post1308420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends.<br /> In this example, the fire breathing example of 'shapeshifted' spells works fine - you do a normal dexterity + .&lt;something&gt; roll to target it, since you also don't use an Arete roll for it. You simply happen to breathe fire, and it's essentially the same as holding a flamethrower weapon in your mouth - it essentially emulates something else that normally wouldn't require an arete roll. Same goes for the shapeshifted ability of forming extra armor or the electricity example from the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, then even offensive attacks can be made with persistent effects. I just don't know how much damage a fire breath would deal in this case. OR how much armor bonus the skin thing wold provide. Maybe according to the successes on the roll?? <br /> <br /> <u><b>The usefulness of Time 4 &quot;hang spell&quot; seems to diminish everytime I think more about persistent effects.</b></u><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1308420#post1308420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth remembering that every Effect a mage has active - all the ones they are &quot;concentrating&quot; on - count towards how difficult it will be to cast additional Effects. Every two simultaneous Effects make the next Effect accrue a +1 difficulty. Hence why Mages don't always have a huge list of Effects they cover themselves with every morning. One or two, maybe. Really, any more than one makes creating Effects in the moment more difficult, and the mage never truly knows all that they'll need beforehand.<br /> <br /> By virtue of being Time 4, a hung effect does not apply here. The Effect isn't present but dormant, like a high-duration one. It exists outside the flow of time entirely, much like an object or creature can be so removed at the same level of mastery. It's not <i>there</i>, until it is.<br /> <br /> This also makes hung Effects harder to detect and, more important, <i>unweaved</i>. A constant Effect is like a beacon to anyone with magickal senses. That makes the Effect vulnerable to attempts to dispel it. Even someone without Prime knowledge could notice some magick is going on, either through other Sphere senses (&quot;the person's biology seems weird somehow&quot;) or through logical deduction given evidence. Hung spells are less likely to be noticed even by the mystically sensitive, because there's no Effect to sense. Yet. Only someone with knowledge of Time could reasonably be expected to spot the irregular knot in the timestream.</div> </div> </div> </div>Persistent effects taht are locked into a target (or self) doens't count as the ones that need concentration and gives the +1 diff in Arete rolls. In M20, mages CAN cover themselves every morning in buffs and effects.<br /> <br /> And as you said, Time 4 spells can be felt by mages with Time. And also can be unweaved too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T06:26:36-07:00","id":1308664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1308512#post1308512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, then even offensive attacks can be made with persistent effects. I just don't know how much damage a fire breath would deal in this case. OR how much armor bonus the skin thing wold provide. Maybe according to the successes on the roll??<br /> <br /> The usefulness of Time 4 &quot;hang spell&quot; seems to diminish everytime I think more about persistent effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>t's an unnatural, potentially Vulgar, modification of your Pattern vs a Spell that wasn't casted yet. This has consequences,<br /> <br /> The Life example of fire-breath costs you Permanent Paradox or Genetic Flaws if it's a permanent modification, or Pattern Bleeding if it isn't permanent. Fire breathing also cost you one point of Quintessence per use (perhaps more, depending on the ST's judgement).<br /> <br /> Time 4 has none of those disadvantages, at the cost of (normaly) being a one-shot thing. And that's why you use Time 4 for Vulgar (or just too evident or inconvenient) circumstantial effects, that are important but you don't *want* to have active all the time and aren't easy to work out as a Wonder.<br /> <br /> A good example it's &quot;post mortem&quot; self-resurrection or vengance curses. These don't make sense to build as an effect built into your Pattern because it's super Vulgar and it only trully matters if you *die*, which it's something you would try to avoid. And because you would try to avoid dying you may not want to expend the resources to create a Wonder (also, depending on how the Wonder works, it could have other disadvantages, like being stealable)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-29-2019, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T08:50:26-07:00","id":1308695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1308664#post1308664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> t's an unnatural, potentially Vulgar, modification of your Pattern vs a Spell that wasn't casted yet. This has consequences,<br /> <br /> The Life example of fire-breath costs you Permanent Paradox or Genetic Flaws if it's a permanent modification, or Pattern Bleeding if it isn't permanent. Fire breathing also cost you one point of Quintessence per use (perhaps more, depending on the ST's judgement).<br /> <br /> Time 4 has none of those disadvantages, at the cost of (normaly) being a one-shot thing. And that's why you use Time 4 for Vulgar (or just too evident or inconvenient) circumstantial effects, that are important but you don't *want* to have active all the time and aren't easy to work out as a Wonder.<br /> <br /> A good example it's &amp;quot;post mortem&amp;quot; self-resurrection or vengance curses. These don't make sense to build as an effect built into your Pattern because it's super Vulgar and it only trully matters if you *die*, which it's something you would try to avoid. And because you would try to avoid dying you may not want to expend the resources to create a Wonder (also, depending on how the Wonder works, it could have other disadvantages, like being stealable)</div> </div> </div> </div>The shapeshifting was just an example that spell with duration doesn't have to be static. <br /> <br /> The shapeshifting will have none of those advantages as long as it last less than 1 day. The quintessence cost is indeed a drawback. But I imagine that the damage would be something according to the successes. So, 6 successes in a ritual, means 3 successes for duration(1 day) and 3 successes for damage, dealing 8 damage (Forces attack) for 1 quint everytime you spit fire for the entire day.<br /> That's way better than casting a hanging fireball with Time 4 that will explode only once.<br /> <br /> Also, maybe you can do that without shapeshifting. Maybe with an effect that when you snap and point your finger at something, a line of flame comes out. It's not a change in your pattern, is a constantly running effect that scan if your are snapping and pointing your finger, and when you do, flames out.<br /> <br /> Also, the resurrection effect you posted csn be made as a persistent effect checking your health, just like the healing pool rote. But instead of wounded it activates when you're dead and instead or healing, it resurrects. Of course, the spheres involved are respective to the effect. And you would need at least 4 successes more to give duration. But that's not so much in a ritual. What you mean with vengance curse?<br /> <br /> I'm trying to find a good enough reason to get Time 4 instead of working intelligently with persistent effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T11:53:09-07:00","id":1308748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The shapeshifting will have none of those advantages as long as it last less than 1 day. The shapeshifting will have none of those advantages as long as it last less than 1 day. The quintessence cost is indeed a drawback. But I imagine that the damage would be something according to the successes. So, 6 successes in a ritual, means 3 successes for duration(1 day) and 3 successes for damage, dealing 8 damage (Forces attack) for 1 quint everytime you spit fire for the entire day.<br /> That's way better than casting a hanging fireball with Time 4 that will explode only once.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's only so many successes you can have before the Ritual starts taking days, this limits what you can do with such a short prep.<br /> <br /> With Time 4 you can prepare a year worth of several different buffs, and release it all when you need them (even several at once). That's much more powerful than your example. And doesn't need Quintessence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, maybe you can do that without shapeshifting. Maybe with an effect that when you snap and point your finger at something, a line of flame comes out. It's not a change in your pattern, is a constantly running effect that scan if your are snapping and pointing your finger, and when you do, flames out. </div> </div> </div>As long as you're <i>locking this on</i> <i>your pattern </i>(which uses Life) it's still a Life pattern alteration, suceptible to all those drawbacks.<br /> <br /> And this example it's against the spirit of Locking. An effect that's constantly running it's <b>an effect </b>(as in, something that <i>affects things</i>) that's constant...the rule wasn't made with the idea of supressing the <i>actual effect</i> under weird triggering conditions. Effects that can be supressed or controled so easily <i>shouldn't</i> get this benefit<br /> <br /> Adding supernatural powers to someone it's Life 5 or Prime 5...if you do that with Locking these powers lack reason to be. So, either the writers made a vile trap to make unintelligent players fall for Life 5, Prime 4-5, etc ... or weren't intending locking to be that powerful or versatile. I don't think I'm crazy by thinking that, RAI, this rule shouldn't allow to do the same things as higher Sphere levels, cheaper, AND with less negative consequences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What you mean with vengance curse? </div> </div> </div>Blowing up your surroundings when you die, for instance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm trying to find a good enough reason to get Time 4 instead of working intelligently with persistent effects. </div> </div> </div>Other than not making your ST mad by trying to exploit the sistem in a way it wasn't intended to be exploited? <br /> <br /> To release Vulgar Great Works on one shot w/o having to carry items or suffer some kind of Permadox seems like it would be using Time 4, even under that heretical take on Locking you have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-29-2019, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T12:16:14-07:00","id":1308754,"title":"","content":"Arguing from rote precedent should be understood to be shaky - beyond edition rules differences, the writers never agree on which determinism is in play. I also think that the tendency to strip examples down into mechanisms is misleading. We shouldn't understand that the ability to turn into a fire-breathing tiger means you can use Matter to create Wonders, even if the situations can be argued to be analogous. It's frustrating, but Mage's magic <i>system </i>isn't particularly <i>systematic</i>.<br /> <br /> That said, the Time 4 (+Entropy 3 optional) rule is old and not well-loved. If you're getting into the legalistic weeds to try and find ways not to do it, just ask your ST to drop it.<br /> <br /> For your specific cites, Gift of Prana isn't really a contingent effect, it uses Prime's ability to enchant living beings to cause the subject's body to be a temporary healing Wonder. Encrypt just looks to be a basic error - the presence of Time 3 is nonsensical, as that level has no bearing on the effect. It's either supposed to be Time 4 or Time 0, by Revised rule (barring one extremely obscure alternative.)<br /> <br /> (Locking is to anchor an effect from a Sphere onto a Pattern governed by a different Sphere, so I don't think you could or would Life-lock a Life effect.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T12:36:46-07:00","id":1308759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1308754#post1308754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Locking is to anchor an effect from a Sphere onto a Pattern governed by a different Sphere, so I don't think you could or would Life-lock a Life effect</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds redundant, and from a certain pov it is redundant, but if you weren't able to lock Life onto your Life pattern...that would mean you would <i>always</i> have to pay the -x penalty to have 2+ temporary Life based buffs (like an increase on your strenght). That doesn't seem to be in the spirit of providing a way out of that penalty, so I would take locking &quot;benefits&quot; to be implicit for those cases.<br /> <br /> About all the rest, I think you're spot on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-29-2019, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T12:59:35-07:00","id":1308764,"title":"","content":"The Locking section in M20 says that same-Pattern effects will often follow their original targets without locking, and only proposes locking as a solution for cross-Sphere working. Do we think it should take Life 2 to maintain a one-dot Life Sense effect without penalties?<br /> <br /> In M20, the following do not apply the juggling penalty:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;an Effect that has a Time-based trigger,<br /> one which has been locked into another Pattern, or one that<br /> has been cast but whose duration has not yet expired, does not<br /> count toward that total. If Lee Ann enchants a guy, and if \u2013<br /> thanks to the number of successes rolled \u2013 that enchantment<br /> lasts for a week after they part company, then Lee Ann does<br /> not have to concentrate on the Effect in order to keep it going.<br /> If she wishes to keep the Effect in motion, however, then it<br /> counts against the number of Effects that character can employ<br /> at the same time.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Which appears to mean that it's actually not just any effect with a Duration - it's one that's being kept in some more active state than merely &quot;going&quot;, though the text doesn't clarify what &quot;keep in motion&quot; means in this instance. It may mean that we're supposed to differentiate between &quot;a spell which makes someone happy for a week&quot; and &quot;a spell which lets me alter someone's mood on command for a week.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T13:12:15-07:00","id":1308769,"title":"","content":"Mmm...I hadn't repared on that. Very interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T20:42:04-07:00","id":1308873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1308748#post1308748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's only so many successes you can have before the Ritual starts taking days, this limits what you can do with such a short prep.<br /> <br /> With Time 4 you can prepare a year worth of several different buffs, and release it all when you need them (even several at once). That's much more powerful than your example. And doesn't need Quintessence.</div> </div> </div> </div>A ceremony is 5-10 successes and each roll reflects an hour. Considering the mage would have to spend at least 3 successes to make it last at least 1 day, there are max 7 successes left. An initial Arete 3 mage that manages to drop the difficulty could make this in what? 3 maybe 4 rolls? This would reflect in 3 or 4 hours a day for a 7 successes effect, which is nice but not the best a ritual can do.<br /> <br /> You've made a good point. I'd say that to make the effect worth it, it has to last more than a day, which means the mage could spend more time gathering successes in the ritual and at least 4 in duration. All this depends on our next topic below:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1308748#post1308748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as you're <i>locking this on</i> <i>your pattern </i>(which uses Life) it's still a Life pattern alteration, suceptible to all those drawbacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it? I thought only direct alteration of the target pattern (the target body, like shapping or changing its body) counted. If a mage wants to turn someone invisible and lock the effect so the target can move invisible (for more than 1 day), that wouldn't cause patter bleeding nor permadox.<br /> <br /> If an effect like this indeed causes pattern bleeding or permadox, I think you have a point and Time 4 is completely worth taking. Spending so many hours every day just to get one powerfull effect like this is not worth it. Also, if the mage wants to have more buffs/running effects, this would take even more time, probably more than a day of rituals, which means it is not possible to do.<br /> <br /> So, those effect should be made to last more than a day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1308748#post1308748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this example it's against the spirit of Locking. An effect that's constantly running it's <b>an effect </b>(as in, something that <i>affects things</i>) that's constant...the rule wasn't made with the idea of supressing the <i>actual effect</i> under weird triggering conditions. <b>Effects that can be supressed or controled so easily <i>shouldn't</i> get this benefit</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> What you mean by the bold quote? I agree that the way effects are presented to us in Mage books are more linear and constant. But there is also no rule preventing them from being dynamic, and we even have examples of some that indeed are, as I posted already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1308748#post1308748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adding supernatural powers to someone it's Life 5 or Prime 5...if you do that with Locking these powers lack reason to be. So, either the writers made a vile trap to make unintelligent players fall for Life 5, Prime 4-5, etc ... or weren't intending locking to be that powerful or versatile. I don't think I'm crazy by thinking that, RAI, this rule shouldn't allow to do the same things as higher Sphere levels, cheaper, AND with less negative consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Life 5 can change Life patterns permanently. You can add supernatural powers way before with Life and probably Forces, depending on the power. The HDYDT example of shapeshifting into the fire-breathing tiger requires Life (3 if it's you, 4 if is someone else) plus Force 3/Prime 2, the regular spheres for creating fire.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T21:17:13-07:00","id":1308881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1308764#post1308764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Locking section in M20 says that same-Pattern effects will often follow their original targets without locking, and only proposes locking as a solution for cross-Sphere working. Do we think it should take Life 2 to maintain a one-dot Life Sense effect without penalties?<br /> <br /> In M20, the following do not apply the juggling penalty:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;an Effect that has a Time-based trigger,<br /> one which has been locked into another Pattern, or one that<br /> has been cast but whose duration has not yet expired, does not<br /> count toward that total. If Lee Ann enchants a guy, and if \u2013<br /> thanks to the number of successes rolled \u2013 that enchantment<br /> lasts for a week after they part company, then Lee Ann does<br /> not have to concentrate on the Effect in order to keep it going.<br /> If she wishes to keep the Effect in motion, however, then it<br /> counts against the number of Effects that character can employ<br /> at the same time.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Which appears to mean that it's actually not just any effect with a Duration - it's one that's being kept in some more active state than merely &quot;going&quot;, though the text doesn't clarify what &quot;keep in motion&quot; means in this instance. It may mean that we're supposed to differentiate between &quot;a spell which makes someone happy for a week&quot; and &quot;a spell which lets me alter someone's mood on command for a week.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, effects that require &quot;concentration&quot; cannot be locked, or will start to count as the ones that will impose a difficulty on Arete as soon as the mage goes on and change it. This might be another evidence that effects doesn't need to be completely statics. &quot;Altering someone's mood on command for a week&quot; is a perfect example of an effect that changes after it is cast. It is not always changing the mood. But I guess this one can't be used with Time 4, and maybe not even locked..<br /> <br /> About the examples I psoted. Well, the gift of prana requiring Prime 3 is odd as well, because to enchant someone into a living charm it is required Prime 4, not 3. And a living wonder doesn't work as a persistent running effect, they are different thing. That rote is an effect not the act of creating a wonder.<br /> <br /> About encrypt we might agree that it indeed looks like an error. I could look for more rotes for examples of constantly running and changing effects, if you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T21:42:12-07:00","id":1308883,"title":"","content":"When I said I don't think generalizing from rote precedent was fruitful, it wasn't a request for <i>more </i>rote precedent. <br /> <br /> Prime enchantment of living beings has unspecified benefits beyond the agg damage standard (consider Rubbing the Bones or whatever), which Prana seems to rely on - fittingly for our discussion, I don't think you could generalize from Prana into a non-Life effect. That's the sort of nuance that I feel gets discarded when you imagine that a specific case can be reduced to a series of necessary mechanisms which can be separated from it and applied elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Let me cut to the chase here:<br /> <br /> HDYDT suggests you can use Life, Forces, and Prime to turn into a fire-breathing tiger. Turning into a tiger is Life 5 (dissimilar mass and size), and creating fire is Forces 3/Prime 2.<br /> <br /> You seem to be concluding from this example that one could, for example, turn a stick into a <i>wand of lightning bolts </i>using Matter 2 (turn a stick into a stick) and Forces 3 / Prime 2.<br /> <br /> I am of the opinion that you probably are not intended to be able to move from the specific to the general in this fashion.<br /> <br /> Effects are not &quot;static&quot; but they generally seem to be &quot;singular&quot;, in the sense that the effect has the traits needed to be the effect specified. A ward's behavior &quot;changes&quot; because the desired effect is necessarily selective, for instance. A flight spell lets you change direction and so on because, well, that's the common-sense expectation of flight. Ascension's magic tends to use degree of success, rather than a mechanical complex of Practices (see Awakening), to differentiate between &quot;complex&quot; and &quot;basic&quot; outcomes.<br /> <br /> Now, you can argue that &quot;I want to create fire on command by pointing my finger&quot; is a singular effect, and if that's cool with your group go for it. In most cases, it seems as though Ascension operates on the notion that you'd just cast the effect each time you wanted to use it - you necessarily have the capacity to, and unlike Awakening there's no inherent mana cost to use magick.<br /> <br /> The intended function of Time/Entropy contingency appears to be based on the idea that, <i>barring effects for which it is obviously necessary, </i>contingent or delayed outcomes require other Spheres, as the delayed (or contingent) release is an embellishment on the singular effect and not an intrinsic trait of the spell.<br /> <br /> No amount of &quot;well <i>this </i>effect seems to allow it without Time&quot; is, to me, useful evidence here, because I think the premise underlying that type of argument is faulty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T17:44:05-07:00","id":1309052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1308883#post1308883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I said I don't think generalizing from rote precedent was fruitful, it wasn't a request for <i>more </i>rote precedent. <br /> <br /> Prime enchantment of living beings has unspecified benefits beyond the agg damage standard (consider Rubbing the Bones or whatever), which Prana seems to rely on - fittingly for our discussion, I don't think you could generalize from Prana into a non-Life effect. That's the sort of nuance that I feel gets discarded when you imagine that a specific case can be reduced to a series of necessary mechanisms which can be separated from it and applied elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Let me cut to the chase here:<br /> <br /> HDYDT suggests you can use Life, Forces, and Prime to turn into a fire-breathing tiger. Turning into a tiger is Life 5 (dissimilar mass and size), and creating fire is Forces 3/Prime 2.<br /> <br /> You seem to be concluding from this example that one could, for example, turn a stick into a <i>wand of lightning bolts </i>using Matter 2 (turn a stick into a stick) and Forces 3 / Prime 2.<br /> <br /> I am of the opinion that you probably are not intended to be able to move from the specific to the general in this fashion.<br /> <br /> Effects are not &amp;quot;static&amp;quot; but they generally seem to be &amp;quot;singular&amp;quot;, in the sense that the effect has the traits needed to be the effect specified. A ward's behavior &amp;quot;changes&amp;quot; because the desired effect is necessarily selective, for instance. A flight spell lets you change direction and so on because, well, that's the common-sense expectation of flight. Ascension's magic tends to use degree of success, rather than a mechanical complex of Practices (see Awakening), to differentiate between &amp;quot;complex&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;basic&amp;quot; outcomes.<br /> <br /> Now, you can argue that &amp;quot;I want to create fire on command by pointing my finger&amp;quot; is a singular effect, and if that's cool with your group go for it. In most cases, it seems as though Ascension operates on the notion that you'd just cast the effect each time you wanted to use it - you necessarily have the capacity to, and unlike Awakening there's no inherent mana cost to use magick.<br /> <br /> The intended function of Time/Entropy contingency appears to be based on the idea that, <i>barring effects for which it is obviously necessary, </i>contingent or delayed outcomes require other Spheres, as the delayed (or contingent) release is an embellishment on the singular effect and not an intrinsic trait of the spell.<br /> <br /> No amount of &amp;quot;well <i>this </i>effect seems to allow it without Time&amp;quot; is, to me, useful evidence here, because I think the premise underlying that type of argument is faulty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Icam more interested in what is doable according to the rules as written, and not on house rules. And to do that, since Mage has a completely free magick system, we need to use tje established rules as well as examples of effects. <br /> A &quot;wand of lightning&quot; would probably be a wonder, or a focus, if we first think about it.<br /> <br /> But if we spend a little time wondering, and I might be wrong here, we can get somewhere :<br /> <br /> Example 1: An area spell that gets whenever who enters very angry. This is a Mind locked effect that is constantly running and when someone enters, another effect is triggered.<br /> <br /> Example 2: an area effect where someone who enters without speaking a password gets put into sleep. That is a locked Mind effect, maybe in conjunction with Forces to detect which sound is being said and if it is the password.<br /> <br /> Example 3: An effect that when the target sneezes he changes the color of his hair. This would be a pure Life effect &quot;locked&quot; in someone.<br /> <br /> Example 4: An enchanted flashlight that when iluminating someone, make the target paralysed. This would be a Forces effect locked in the flashlight with Matter. I know this may be a wonder, but I'm working at the possibility of being an effect.<br /> <br /> So, are any of these effects doable? Are the spheres right? I don't see Time 4 going in any of those.<br /> <br /> Also, do you agree that constantly running buffs can be made just like the prana rote? Instead of healing, buffing some trait.<br /> <br /> Aleph already made a good point about rituals complications that might turn this impracticable, but I'd like to wonder about it.<br /> <br /> Also, do you think any of those effects would result in pattern bleeding or permadox?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T21:41:02-07:00","id":1309095,"title":"","content":"The horrible truth is that all I can offer are, effectively, <i>my </i>table rules - a lot of this stuff is negotiated at the table, ranging from the vulgarity of effects to how complicated an effect is, or even how many Sphere dots it requires. I'll try to be supportive, but allow me to reiterate: This isn't stuff we have hard rules on, and I don't think we ever will. I can only offer interpretations.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> <b>First example: </b>Projecting emotions is Mind 2. No need to lock if the area is intended to be stationary. Probably would be an &quot;ongoing&quot; effect, causing the juggling penalty, if the influence remains in place and would affect people entering the area after the mage has left - that's based on my read of the section I quoted earlier in the thread.<br /> <br /> <b>Second example: </b>By HDYDT's overlong section on wards, this would be Corr 4 (the ward), Matter 2 (locked to a passageway), Life or Mind ~3 (sleep effect), and probably Forces to detect the password. With Mind 4, you could have the ward target selected types of mind - this would mean that people who know the password would not be affected, and would not have to say it aloud, which would allow you to drop the Forces requirement. Obviously 10+ dots of Spheres is a lot to achieve this relatively unambitious effect, but near as I can tell that's how it runs by the book in M20. I'd do it differently at my table.<br /> <br /> The alternative is to say &quot;well it's <i>like </i>a ward, but it's not a <i>ward-ward&quot; </i>which is going to require your ST to agree that &quot;a spell to protect a region that has an effect on people who trespass&quot; is meaningfully distinct from &quot;a ward.&quot; A nonselective sleep spell locked to a doorway is like Mind or Life 3/Matter 2.<br /> <br /> <b>Third example: </b>Uncontrolled cosmetic alteration of another person? Life 3, probably. You don't have to lock Life to Life, as I've said above.<br /> <br /> &quot;Cause his hair to change color the next time he takes a shower&quot; seems to be Life 3/Time 4/Entropy 3 in M20.<br /> <br /> <b>Fourth example: </b>Locking allows an effect to travel along with a nonstandard Pattern. Paralysis is some sort of Life or Mind or etc, probably in the 3-4 dot range.<br /> <br /> Locking it to the flashlight with Matter would presumably make it affect anyone touching the flashlight, or have the effect radiate in all directions from the flashlight. Locking it to the flashlight's <i>beam </i>with Forces could cause it to work on whoever it was directed at, but turning the flashlight off would, in my estimation, end the effect - the Pattern carrying the spell would be gone.</div> <br /> Gift of Prana leverages some of the nonmechanical &quot;benefits&quot; of Prime enchantment of living bodies, so you might build effects which are analogous - but because the effect of Prime on living beings is mostly, like, a rush of energy or improved well-being, most of what you'd want to do could be done with Life directly, or maybe some very minor mood-based Mind stuff. There are old effects which suggest you can use Prime's effect on living bodies to cause bliss, improve health, correct imbalance, or inflict pain. As an example, I'd allow this:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b><i>The Corrective Lotus Fist (Life 3/Prime 3): </i></b>By striking key acupoints corresponding to the water system within a subject's body, Akashic masters enchants them to protect against toxic effects. The enchantment costs 1 quint (as standard for enchant life) and uses Life to attempt to countermand drugs or poisons the subject is exposed to. Though this has practical applications, it is most often used on disciples - wayward apprentices that sneak out of the temple to drink find themselves sobering up at impossible speed. The more exacting Akashic masters opt <i>not </i>to provide protection against the rapid-onset hangover which results.</div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T13:46:23-07:00","id":1309277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1309095#post1309095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The horrible truth is that all I can offer are, effectively, <i>my </i>table rules - a lot of this stuff is negotiated at the table, ranging from the vulgarity of effects to how complicated an effect is, or even how many Sphere dots it requires. I'll try to be supportive, but allow me to reiterate: This isn't stuff we have hard rules on, and I don't think we ever will. I can only offer interpretations.</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> <br /> Yes, I am aware of that and I understand completely. As I said, since Mage magick is so freeform, we can only base in some book rules and examples, which is not enough to have something 100% concrete and things will vary from table to table. Still, I really like to see other people arguments and ways of view of the rules and I hope that you guys don't mind giving them for someone as stubborn as I am.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1309095#post1309095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>First example: </b>Projecting emotions is Mind 2. No need to lock if the area is intended to be stationary. Probably would be an &quot;ongoing&quot; effect, causing the juggling penalty, if the influence remains in place and would affect people entering the area after the mage has left - that's based on my read of the section I quoted earlier in the thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, when I said locked I meant persistent, with a duration. But I don't think it would count as &quot;ongoing&quot; as long as it has a duration and the mage doesn't want to change the effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1309095#post1309095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Second example: </b>By HDYDT's overlong section on wards, this would be Corr 4 (the ward), Matter 2 (locked to a passageway), Life or Mind ~3 (sleep effect), and probably Forces to detect the password. With Mind 4, you could have the ward target selected types of mind - this would mean that people who know the password would not be affected, and would not have to say it aloud, which would allow you to drop the Forces requirement. Obviously 10+ dots of Spheres is a lot to achieve this relatively unambitious effect, but near as I can tell that's how it runs by the book in M20. I'd do it differently at my table.<br /> <br /> The alternative is to say &quot;well it's <i>like </i>a ward, but it's not a <i>ward-ward&quot; </i>which is going to require your ST to agree that &quot;a spell to protect a region that has an effect on people who trespass&quot; is meaningfully distinct from &quot;a ward.&quot; A nonselective sleep spell locked to a doorway is like Mind or Life 3/Matter 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>A ward is made to prevent someone to enter/touch/etc. some place/thing. I guess that's why Correspondence is needed. Either way, being a Ward or not, you agree that it doesn't require Time 4 and it has a condition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1309095#post1309095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Third example: </b>Uncontrolled cosmetic alteration of another person? Life 3, probably. You don't have to lock Life to Life, as I've said above.<br /> <br /> &quot;Cause his hair to change color the next time he takes a shower&quot; seems to be Life 3/Time 4/Entropy 3 in M20.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Yes, again my mistake. No need to lock, just give it a duration. But what if instead of sneezing it is shouting? Or bitting his tongue? And instead of changing hair, release a wave of kinectic energy from his body? Would it be Life 2 (to lock and check if his tongue is bitten) and Forces 2 to release the wave?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1309095#post1309095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Fourth example: </b>Locking allows an effect to travel along with a nonstandard Pattern. Paralysis is some sort of Life or Mind or etc, probably in the 3-4 dot range.<br /> <br /> Locking it to the flashlight with Matter would presumably make it affect anyone touching the flashlight, or have the effect radiate in all directions from the flashlight. Locking it to the flashlight's <i>beam </i>with Forces could cause it to work on whoever it was directed at, but turning the flashlight off would, in my estimation, end the effect - the Pattern carrying the spell would be gone.</div> </div> </div> </div></div>I see. Then you believe it's not possible to attach the effect into the action of turning the light on without making it a wonder. Or locking into the beam, which would require the flashlight to be always on in turn to keep the effect active, which would result in constantly paralysing anyone that is illuminated. Fair enough.<br /> <br /> What is your take on pattern bleeding and permadox in those effects, like the Life ones I gave?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T22:39:40-07:00","id":1309379,"title":"","content":"My rule of thumb here is:<br /> <br /> 1.) &quot;Is the effect always on, even if its effects are not currently relevant.&quot;<br /> <br /> Consider a Mind spell which makes it impossible to talk about Dave. It's not contingent or delayed, even if it's necessarily selective. Or a Life-locked Forces effect which softens someone's falls, which just isn't doing something while they aren't falling.<br /> <br /> 2.) &quot;Is the supposed trigger an inherent quality of the effect, or a convenience to delay the effect until desired?&quot;<br /> <br /> Consider the difference between a Life-locked Forces effect which amplifies the subject's shouts into a deafening sonic blast, and a Time-delayed Entropy-triggered Corr spell which teleports the mage home when they shout. This is another example of what I mean about not being able to project forward &quot;precedent&quot; from one case to another. Identical activation cases may not require identical Sphere use.<br /> <br /> I think your notion of using an conjunctional Sphere to &quot;detect&quot; a trigger is reaching - I don't you've done anything to support it, and the very fact that it <i>does </i>almostcompletely invalidate Time triggers would suggest it to be suspect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What is your take on pattern bleeding and permadox in those effects, like the Life ones I gave? </div> </div> </div>Pattern bleed is a consequence of lasting radical changes to a Life pattern - superhuman faculties, new limbs, etc. I don't think anything we've discussed really runs into that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T05:32:26-07:00","id":1309416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1309379#post1309379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pattern bleed is a consequence of lasting radical changes to a Life pattern - superhuman faculties, new limbs, etc. I don't think anything we've discussed really runs into that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that what Lord Revan it's asking if it's locking an effect that's not a purely Life based enhancement <i>can </i>get Pattern Bleeding or Permadox.<br /> <br /> I get that changing hair color shouldn't get that, probably...but what about, say, making your hair constantly emit a halo of sunlight (Prime/Forces locked into Life) or giving yourself superman's laser-sight and flight with the &quot;complex&quot; locking mechanisms suggested by Revan. And make those alterations lasting, of course<br /> <br /> Personally, I would think that adding such capabilities to a pattern <i>has</i> to have some reaction from Unbelief, since they're quite supernatural. Doing so it's a pretty constant &quot;in your face&quot; to Reality that's now residing on your Life pattern. I tought reasonable for an alteration like that resulting in those sort of penalties until the *thing* get's off, since that's exactly the sort of supernatural enhancements that it was created to discourage (giving you persistent wings to fly makes your pattern bleed, but giving you persistent <i>superman style flight</i> doesn't't?).<br /> <br /> I took &quot;direct alteration of the target pattern&quot; as something that would also apply to other Spheres having your Life pattern as a medium (the direct radical alteration would be having the Spheres shooting their reality blasting effects <i>trough your pattern</i>), but perhaps I AM interpreting that part too freely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-02-2019, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T19:06:44-07:00","id":1309557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1309379#post1309379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My rule of thumb here is:<br /> <br /> 1.) &quot;Is the effect always on, even if its effects are not currently relevant.&quot;<br /> <br /> Consider a Mind spell which makes it impossible to talk about Dave. It's not contingent or delayed, even if it's necessarily selective. Or a Life-locked Forces effect which softens someone's falls, which just isn't doing something while they aren't falling.<br /> <br /> 2.) &quot;Is the supposed trigger an inherent quality of the effect, or a convenience to delay the effect until desired?&quot;<br /> <br /> Consider the difference between a Life-locked Forces effect which amplifies the subject's shouts into a deafening sonic blast, and a Time-delayed Entropy-triggered Corr spell which teleports the mage home when they shout. This is another example of what I mean about not being able to project forward &quot;precedent&quot; from one case to another. Identical activation cases may not require identical Sphere use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent examples!! I see that your teleport one was the only that required Time 4. In my understending, all of them are constantly running (the teleporting one isn't, but maybe it could). But as for your desccription in #2 you consider the effect is not always running. Why is the ssoft falling effect always running and the amplified shout not?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1309379#post1309379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pattern bleed is a consequence of lasting radical changes to a Life pattern - superhuman faculties, new limbs, etc. I don't think anything we've discussed really runs into that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with you in this one. Pattern bleeding/permadox are only for direct changes into the body pattern of the mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T19:40:09-07:00","id":1309562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1309416#post1309416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that what Lord Revan it's asking if it's locking an effect that's not a purely Life based enhancement <i>can </i>get Pattern Bleeding or Permadox.<br /> <br /> I get that changing hair color shouldn't get that, probably...but what about, say, making your hair constantly emit a halo of sunlight (Prime/Forces locked into Life) or giving yourself superman's laser-sight and flight with the &quot;complex&quot; locking mechanisms suggested by Revan. And make those alterations lasting, of course<br /> <br /> Personally, I would think that adding such capabilities to a pattern <i>has</i> to have some reaction from Unbelief, since they're quite supernatural. Doing so it's a pretty constant &quot;in your face&quot; to Reality that's now residing on your Life pattern. I tought reasonable for an alteration like that resulting in those sort of penalties until the *thing* get's off, since that's exactly the sort of supernatural enhancements that it was created to discourage (giving you persistent wings to fly makes your pattern bleed, but giving you persistent <i>superman style flight</i> doesn't't?).<br /> <br /> I took &quot;direct alteration of the target pattern&quot; as something that would also apply to other Spheres having your Life pattern as a medium (the direct radical alteration would be having the Spheres shooting their reality blasting effects <i>trough your pattern</i>), but perhaps I AM interpreting that part too freely.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Changing hair color isn't a radical change of someone's body. It is not vulgar either. A halo of sunlight definitely is and if it is going to last more than a day I agree that pattern bleeding should apply.<br /> Now, the Forces effects aren't changing the mage's body. They are just locked. By your logic, any effect that is locked for more than a day will generate pattern bleeding. I think you are mistaken.<br /> Paradox is a high enough price to pay for such effects. About the wings example, I don't know, maybe flying superman style requires concentration while wings doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T20:40:01-07:00","id":1309570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1309416#post1309416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that what Lord Revan it's asking if it's locking an effect that's not a purely Life based enhancement <i>can </i>get Pattern Bleeding or Permadox.<br /> <br /> I get that changing hair color shouldn't get that, probably...but what about, say, making your hair constantly emit a halo of sunlight (Prime/Forces locked into Life) or giving yourself superman's laser-sight and flight with the &quot;complex&quot; locking mechanisms suggested by Revan. And make those alterations lasting, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aha! I think I have grasped the question now.<br /> <br /> Enduring magickal or hypertech adjustments can cause permadox, and magickal superpowers would definitely fit the bill. In <i>addition </i>to that, lasting radical changes to a Life pattern can cause pattern bleeding. I wouldn't think of Life-locked effects as being radical changes to the Pattern (they ride along, but they're not changing the body), so I think in M20 they wouldn't cause Pattern bleeding, but they might cause permadox. Using a long-lasting Life effect to give yourself tiger claws or wings could reasonably cause <i>both.</i><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i><b>Sunlight hair</b></i>: Permadox, probably no Pattern bleed.<br /> <i><b>Superhuman Strength</b></i>: Permadox and Pattern bleed.<br /> <i><b>Modest increase in Strength (within one dot of your real stat)</b></i>: Pattern bleed but no permadox.</div> <br /> (In Revised, there's a neutral analog to the Technocratic Enhancements background, called Blessing, which is often balanced by Flaws in the way that Enhancements is. Blessing exists in M20 but has a very different effect.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1309557#post1309557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellent examples!! I see that your teleport one was the only that required Time 4. In my understending, all of them are constantly running (the teleporting one isn't, but maybe it could). But as for your desccription in #2 you consider the effect is not always running. Why is the ssoft falling effect always running and the amplified shout not?</div> </div> </div> </div>The amplified shout is intended to meet both of the criteria - it's always on (speak softly), and while it's not always *active*, the thing which causes the effect to be relevant is clearly tied to what the effect is.<br /> <br /> Near as I can tell, the use case for Time suspension in M20 is when you need a lasting delay (it implies that Entr3 triggers will be held indefinitely) or when you want magic on command. I think your examples of &quot;telling the spell what to do&quot; with pointing, etc. tend to fall into the magic on command bucket, and my criteria are intended to differentiate between &quot;it would be convenient for this effect to be delayed&quot; and &quot;by its nature, this effect is always on but not always active.&quot;<br /> <br /> It seems that in M20, having infernal fire engulf someone who points a gun at you is Forces/Prime/Time/Entropy. It doesn't seem to be the case that you could use Mind or Matter to &quot;detect&quot; the hostile gun and &quot;tell&quot; a Forces/Prime effect to take place.<br /> <br /> You might have a Life-locked Matter effect that causes the mechanisms of guns around you to not work, though, and that does not seem to require Time - it's doesn't discriminate (it's not on-command, your gun would be affected too, etc.), it's always on, and its &quot;active&quot; condition is clearly related to the desired effect.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T22:10:40-07:00","id":1309572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1309570#post1309570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aha! I think I have grasped the question now.<br /> <br /> Enduring magickal or hypertech adjustments can cause permadox, and magickal superpowers would definitely fit the bill. In <i>addition </i>to that, lasting radical changes to a Life pattern can cause pattern bleeding. I wouldn't think of Life-locked effects as being radical changes to the Pattern (they ride along, but they're not changing the body), so I think in M20 they wouldn't cause Pattern bleeding, but they might cause permadox. Using a long-lasting Life effect to give yourself tiger claws or wings could reasonably cause <i>both.</i><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i><b>Sunlight hair</b></i>: Permadox, probably no Pattern bleed.<br /> <i><b>Superhuman Strength</b></i>: Permadox and Pattern bleed.<br /> <i><b>Modest increase in Strength (within one dot of your real stat)</b></i>: Pattern bleed but no permadox.</div><br /> (In Revised, there's a neutral analog to the Technocratic Enhancements background, called Blessing, which is often balanced by Flaws in the way that Enhancements is. Blessing exists in M20 but has a very different effect.)</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as i know, permanent paradox only comes in play with Enhancements or a radical change in your pattern is made permanent. And having those radical changes more than 1 day, but not permanently, result only in pattern bleeding. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1309570#post1309570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The amplified shout is intended to meet both of the criteria - it's always on (speak softly), and while it's not always *active*, the thing which causes the effect to be relevant is clearly tied to what the effect is.<br /> <br /> Near as I can tell, the use case for Time suspension in M20 is when you need a lasting delay (it implies that Entr3 triggers will be held indefinitely) or when you want magic on command. I think your examples of &quot;telling the spell what to do&quot; with pointing, etc. tend to fall into the magic on command bucket, and my criteria are intended to differentiate between &quot;it would be convenient for this effect to be delayed&quot; and &quot;by its nature, this effect is always on but not always active.&quot;<br /> <br /> It seems that in M20, having infernal fire engulf someone who points a gun at you is Forces/Prime/Time/Entropy. It doesn't seem to be the case that you could use Mind or Matter to &quot;detect&quot; the hostile gun and &quot;tell&quot; a Forces/Prime effect to take place.<br /> <br /> You might have a Life-locked Matter effect that causes the mechanisms of guns around you to not work, though, and that does not seem to require Time - it's doesn't discriminate (it's not on-command, your gun would be affected too, etc.), it's always on, and its &quot;active&quot; condition is clearly related to the desired effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Then all the 3 effects are indeed constantly &quot;running&quot;, they just happens to be doing nothing while the mage isn't shouting (or falling, or talking about Dave, depending on the example). And when the &quot;trigger&quot;has nothing to do with the effect, like a shout activating a teleportation, then it would require Time 4.<br /> <br /> This makes sense. And it seems that it is pretty much how the rotes I used as examples do. The effect is kept always running and the trigger is related to the effect. Gift of prana keeps running and whenever you are hurt, it heals you.(both related to health) Encrypt is always running and whenever you are interrogated you can't speak (both related to trading information). They are somewhat related.<br /> <br /> We indeed have no evidence of the use of other spheres as triggers as I suggested, then I guess it will fall into ST decision to allow it.<br /> <br /> But, this means you agree that when it comes to buffs, they can be done without Time 4, even being activated by some related condition (like gift of prana). For buffs, then, we still have no advantages on using Time 4.<br /> <br /> Quick question: does the Time 4 hang must be casted in the same spell, in the same Arete roll? Or it can be like 2 Arete rolls in 2 different turns?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T00:19:15-07:00","id":1309588,"title":"","content":"Regarding permanent paradox: The relevant section is on 548 of M20, and makes no mention of permanence. Same holds for Revised, where the perma-dox only lasts for as long as the change is maintained (Revised provides the standard of &quot;superhuman faculty&quot; that I'm thinking of.) If HDYDT disagrees, take a shot and flip a coin, I guess.<br /> <br /> Time's marginal for any indiscriminate buff you could safely maintain, yes. Not all buffs are subtle or safe enough to have running - an invisibility effect or Force field would interfere with normal day-to-day living, for example. It seems in M20 there's a further benefit to Time/Ent triggers, where the spell will be suspended indefinitely until needed (instead of caring about the duration factor - this is how the language in the Time sphere section looks, and the writer of the Ward section in HDYDT appears to believe so, too.) Rather like its D&amp;D counterpart, spell triggers and contingencies are for things you want to release quickly and/or in response to an emergency, such as storing a protracted casting of a powerful Forces effect to unleash when threatened - or using the example Time case of holding a tornado in a time pocket as a bargaining chip. I could see a Hermetic Adept having that rote from their Tradbook that blows guns up held in a contingent trigger - it'd be great insurance, and in M20 it appears you could cast it once and leave it running for weeks or months without worry.<br /> <br /> The Time trigger is referred to as being &quot;in conjunction with&quot; other Spheres, so it would be the same spell and Arete roll. That said, Time 4 seems like it would also be adequate to &quot;bottle up&quot; an existing spell as a separate effect, with its own Arete roll and duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T05:22:45-07:00","id":1309623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1309562#post1309562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changing hair color isn't a radical change of someone's body. It is not vulgar either. A halo of sunlight definitely is and if it is going to last more than a day I agree that pattern bleeding should apply.<br /> Now, the Forces effects aren't changing the mage's body. They are just locked. By your logic, any effect that is locked for more than a day will generate pattern bleeding. I think you are mistaken.<br /> Paradox is a high enough price to pay for such effects. About the wings example, I don't know, maybe flying superman style requires concentration while wings doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Enduring magickal or hypertech adjustments can cause permadox, and magickal superpowers would definitely fit the bill. In <i>addition </i>to that, lasting radical changes to a Life pattern can cause pattern bleeding. I wouldn't think of Life-locked effects as being radical changes to the Pattern (they ride along, but they're not changing the body), so I think in M20 they wouldn't cause Pattern bleeding, but they might cause permadox. Using a long-lasting Life effect to give yourself tiger claws or wings could reasonably cause <i>both.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Those are good arguments, and conditional permadox it's a high enough price for any Vulgarity. <br /> <br /> It DOES make Life argumentations a little lackluster (being hit with both hammers), but then you use only one Sphere for them, while locking takes at least 2. So I guess in a sense you already paid for the bleeding","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T10:33:24-07:00","id":1309682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1309588#post1309588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding permanent paradox: The relevant section is on 548 of M20, and makes no mention of permanence. Same holds for Revised, where the perma-dox only lasts for as long as the change is maintained (Revised provides the standard of &amp;quot;superhuman faculty&amp;quot; that I'm thinking of.) If HDYDT disagrees, take a shot and flip a coin, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right. Radical change into own pattern result in permadox as long as it is on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1309588#post1309588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time's marginal for any indiscriminate buff you could safely maintain, yes. Not all buffs are subtle or safe enough to have running - an invisibility effect or Force field would interfere with normal day-to-day living, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then we will go back to the shapeshifting thing. Without Time 4, the magr have 2 options: shapeshift into an invisible activated by will human and get permadox/pattern bleed, or use a locked effect and roll with the side effects. <br /> It seems fair and Time 4 looks much better now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1309588#post1309588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems in M20 there's a further benefit to Time/Ent triggers, where the spell will be suspended indefinitely until needed (instead of caring about the duration factor - this is how the language in the Time sphere section looks, and the writer of the Ward section in HDYDT appears to believe so, too.) Rather like its D&amp;D counterpart, spell triggers and contingencies are for things you want to release quickly and/or in response to an emergency, such as storing a protracted casting of a powerful Forces effect to unleash when threatened - or using the example Time case of holding a tornado in a time pocket as a bargaining chip. I could see a Hermetic Adept having that rote from their Tradbook that blows guns up held in a contingent trigger - it'd be great insurance, and in M20 it appears you could cast it once and leave it running for weeks or months without worry.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't get the tornado example. But yeah, releasing lots of powerful effects in one turn looks pretty cool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307929-hanging-spells-time-4?p=1309588#post1309588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Time trigger is referred to as being &amp;quot;in conjunction with&amp;quot; other Spheres, so it would be the same spell and Arete roll. That said, Time 4 seems like it would also be adequate to &amp;quot;bottle up&amp;quot; an existing spell as a separate effect, with its own Arete roll and duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. It is according to the caster's intent, then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}